blurb: The South Portland School Board held a public forum to discuss the challenging
  FY27 budget, driven by declining student enrollment and rising costs. Potential
  solutions, including elementary school reconfiguration and operational efficiencies,
  were presented for community feedback to address a projected $7.2 million budget
  gap.
